l Duties & Responsibilities Daily Responsibilities Post online giving donations. Confirm and reconcile third-party gift information in online portals. Review Informer reports for address updates and biographical changes. Review newspaper articles for RC community mentions. Review obituary data for RC community. Weekly Responsibilities Prepare and distribute Commemoration Cards. Seasonal Responsibilities Create parent records for newly deposited students. Assist with biographic data verification during Giving Days. Required Qualifications Associate degree required; bachelor’s degree preferred. Must be available for in-person daytime work hours. Due to the nature of the schedule, candidates cannot be enrolled in an in-person academic program. Knowledge, Skills & Competencies Accountability: Takes ownership of tasks and follows through consistently. Attention to Detail: Ensures accuracy in data entry and record maintenance. Responsibility: Demonstrates reliability and professionalism in all duties. Conscientiousness: Completes work thoroughly and with care. Trustworthiness: Handles confidential information appropriately. Technical Proficiency: Ability to learn and navigate RC systems including Colleague, CRM Advance, Informer, and online portals such as GiveCampus and AlumniFinder. Preferred Experience Experience working in an office environment with standard administrative technology and tools. Familiarity with data entry, record management, or CRM/database systems. Comfort navigating online platforms used for research, verification, or information review. Prior experience using organizational email and productivity software to support daily workflow. Ability to learn new systems and tools quickly and apply them accurately in routine tasks. Physical Requirements Ability to remain seated or at a workstation for extended periods. Ability to move within the office environment, including lobby coverage. Ability to lift up to 10 pounds occasionally (files, small office supplies). Ability to read printed and digital materials for data review. Ability to perform repetitive tasks such as typing and data entry. Work Environment Standard office environment. In-person role requiring consistent attendance. Shared responsibility for lobby coverage with the Executive Assistant. Additional Information This position supports the Advancement Office’s commitment to maintaining accurate donor and constituent information and ensuring smooth daily operations. The role requires professionalism, discretion, and a high level of accuracy Return to Roanoke College Apply for this job Apply for this job Apply for this job SHARE Not the right job? Join our Talent Network Location Return to Roanoke College POWERED BY APPLICANT TRACKING"
