ning student check-in; monitors students’ check-in completion and sends reminders as appropriate; communicates with Business Office when late check-in fees are to be assessed Processes all withdrawals from the College; provides weekly reporting on withdrawals to appropriate offices; corresponds with former students planning to return to the College; reactivates records of former returning students Prepares and submits diploma orders; prepares the list of prospective graduates for the commencement program and works with the Marketing and Communications Department on the preparation of the commencement program Maintains the department budget and all pertinent files; processes reimbursement requests and invoice approvals for Registrar budget Uses Entrinsik Informer for reporting for the Registrar’s Office as well as other departments Serves as a resource to students regarding the Intellectual Inquiry program requirements and related substitutions Completes transfer credit evaluations in the absence of the Registrar Prepares the academic calendar for each term and academic year and posts the calendar to the RC webpage Monitors academic calendar deadlines Maintains the Registrar’s Office webpage; monitors web settings so that appropriate terms are available for viewing and registration Serves as the liaison between the Registrar’s Office and the Office of Institutional Research and the Information Technology office Serves as liaison between the College and the Veterans Administration Performs other duties as assigned Education, Experience, Skills, and Abilities : Bachelor’s degree required Expertise in use of the Ellucian Colleague Student Information System Return to Roanoke College Apply for this job Apply for this job Apply for this job SHARE Not the right job? Join our Talent Network Location Return to Roanoke College POWERED BY APPLICANT TRACKING"
